# Two Spacers share what the row leaves: 77 cells at 80 columns, so the earlier takes the odd
# cell (docs/design/primitives/stacks.md). `Spacer(minLength: 20)` makes no difference here,
# since a share is already 39; stacks-mobile.scn is where its floor binds. The Spacer in the
# three-row VStack is the one row between `A` and `B`. `s` steps the spacing of the first row,
# `v` puts a blank row between the lines of the three VStacks.
app stacks
size desktop

expect text 2 "A B C spacing 1"
expect node type=HStack nth=0 frame 0,2,15x1
expect node type=Spacer nth=0 frame 24,9,0x1
expect node type=Spacer nth=1 frame 1,13,78x0
expect node type=Spacer nth=2 frame 1,15,39x0
expect node type=Spacer nth=3 frame 41,15,38x0
expect node type=Spacer nth=4 frame 1,17,39x0
expect node type=Spacer nth=5 frame 41,17,38x0
check
shot desktop

key s
expect text 2 "A  B  C  spacing 2"
expect node type=HStack nth=0 frame 0,2,18x1

key v
expect node type=VStack nth=2 frame 0,4,7x5
expect node type=Spacer nth=1 frame 1,15,78x0
check
shot rows-apart
